yula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"type":"inland archaeological day-trip - no overnight lodging market; based from Tulum/Playa","peak":"Nov-Apr dry season (fewer mosquitoes, less heat/humidity); April standout; Dec-Jan busier (Riviera Maya high season)","shoulder":"May + Oct","green":"Jun-Sep (jungle heat/humidity peak, hurricane-season afternoon rain) - go at 8:00 AM opening","demand_driver":"Nohoch Mul climb REOPENED Dec 8, 2025 (42 m, groups of 15, 15-min limit, closed-toe shoes); VERIFY still open at booking","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"N/A on-site (no beds); anchor Coba day trip to a coastal Tulum/Playa/Riviera Maya stay; sell cave-cenote swims as heat counterweight","sources":["https://www.besttime2travel.com/coba","https://www.chichenitza.com/blog/nohoch-mul-the-tallest-temple-in-coba","https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/coba-ruins-guide/"],"fire_date":"fire inside the coastal booking cycle (Aug-Oct winter peak; Feb-Mar shoulder); lead with ''Nohoch Mul is climbable again''","event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year, Semana Santa (arrive 8:00 AM); post-reopening Nohoch Mul climb demand","booking_lead":"day-trip/excursion booking (days to weeks); no overnight market; bed-night lead time sits on the Tulum/Playa base"},"jewels":[{"name":"Nohoch Mul pyramid climb","si_tag":"Culture & Heritage","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"INAH entry + guided ruins tour","source":"https://www.chichenitza.com/blog/nohoch-mul-the-tallest-temple-in-coba","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"one of the tallest Maya pyramids, reopened Dec 2025 via protective wooden staircase; jungle-canopy summit view","si":"culture","blurb":"one of the tallest Maya pyramids, reopened Dec 2025 via protective wooden staircase; jungle-canopy summit view","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"Amstar/Olympus DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary","expedition":"destination","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Coba archaeological zone by bike/pedicab","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"guided tour + on-site bike/pedicab rental","source":"https://www.mexicotravelandleisure.com/blog/coba-ruins-guide/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"sprawling jungle Maya city linked by ancient white sacbé roads; cover it by bicycle or pedicab","si":"expedition","blurb":"sprawling jungle Maya city linked by ancient white sacbé roads; cover it by bicycle or pedicab","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture","expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"evidenced","expedition":"primary","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Choo-Ha cave cenote","si_tag":"Family","status":"future","tier":"essential","bookable":"cenote entry + combo tour","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/coba-cenotes/","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"shallow, stalactite-filled cavern; the gentlest of the three — good family/first-cenote swim","si":"family","blurb":"shallow, stalactite-filled cavern; the gentlest of the three — good family/first-cenote swim","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate (entry non-commissionable)","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["family"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"destination","family":"primary"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Tankach-Ha cave cenote","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"cenote entry + combo tour","source":"https://www.mexicocenotesandruins.com/cenote-tankach-ha-coba/","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"deep cavern with 5 m & 10 m jump platforms and dramatic stalactites","si":"expedition","blurb":"deep cavern with 5 m & 10 m jump platforms and dramatic stalactites","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Multun-Ha cave cenote","si_tag":"Global Expedition Adventures","status":"live","tier":"essential","bookable":"cenote entry + combo tour","source":"https://bucketlistbri.com/coba-cenotes/","timing":"Nov-Apr dry season","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the third, quieter cave cenote in the Cobá cluster; cool clear underground pool","si":"expedition","blurb":"the third, quieter cave cenote in the Cobá cluster; cool clear underground pool","when":"Nov-Apr dry season","commission":"DMC + Viator affiliate","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["expedition"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"destination","expedition":"primary","family":"destination"},"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for at Cobá?","a":"Heat and hydration, plus mosquitoes — not crime. Cobá is open, humid jungle with a 42 m pyramid climb, so the main risk is heat exhaustion: go at the 8:00 AM opening, carry ample water and sun protection. Dengue is active — Quintana Roo is among Mexico''s highest-activity states in 2026 — so use repellent; there is effectively no malaria.","source":"nomadoc.com.mx / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Can you climb Nohoch Mul in 2026?","a":"Yes — climbing reopened on December 8, 2025 after roughly six years closed, so verify it is still open at booking. A new wooden staircase now protects the original 120 stone steps up to the 42 m (138 ft) summit, one of the tallest Maya pyramids, with a jungle-canopy view from the top. Climb window is 8:00 AM–3:30 PM.","source":"chichenitza.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"How do you get around Cobá, and how far is it from the coast?","a":"By bicycle or pedicab — the site is too vast to walk comfortably. Cobá sits ~47 km (29 mi) NW of Tulum, so it is almost always done as a guided day trip from a Tulum, Playa del Carmen or Riviera Maya base; it has essentially no overnight lodging market of its own. The zone opens at 8:00 AM.","source":"xamanhaconnections.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Are the Cobá cenotes good for kids?","a":"Yes — the cave cenotes make an ideal cool-off after the ruins. Choo-Ha is shallow and gentle, the best first cenote for children; all three have safety ropes and provided life jackets. Shower off sunscreen before entering to protect the water, and take the steep, wet stone stairs carefully (Tankach-Ha is ~83 steps down).","source":"bucketlistbri.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"family"},{"q":"When is the best time to visit Cobá?","a":"November–April, the dry season, is best — fewer mosquitoes, lower humidity and less heat for the jungle climb, with April the standout month. Whatever the season, arrive at the 8:00 AM opening to beat both the heat and the crowds; the June–September green season brings peak jungle heat and hurricane-season afternoon rain.","source":"besttime2travel.com / mexicotravelandleisure.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"planning"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cobá Ruins & Cenotes: Climb Nohoch Mul","meta_description":"Cobá is inland Maya jungle — climb the 42 m Nohoch Mul pyramid (reopened Dec 2025) and swim the Choo-Ha, Tankach-Ha and Multun-Ha cave cenotes. When, fees and safety.","slug":"coba-mexico","primary_keyword":"Cobá ruins","long_tail":["Nohoch Mul climbing 2026","Coba cenotes Choo-Ha Tankach-Ha","Coba ruins from Tulum","tallest Maya pyramid Quintana Roo","Coba bike pedicab jungle ruins"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["ruinas de Cobá","subir Nohoch Mul Cobá reabierto","pirámide más alta maya Quintana Roo","cenotes Cobá Choo-Ha Tankach-Ha Multun-Ha","Cobá desde Tulum","tour Cobá y cenotes","bicicleta bicitaxi ruinas de Cobá"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.Worl