ndy beaches and small colonial homes rather than high-rises","si":"romance","blurb":"Colonia''s boardwalk fronts sandy beaches and small colonial homes rather than high-rises","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"content anchor — drives boutique-hotel + dining revenue","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture","romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"evidenced","romance":"primary"},"commission_lane":["hotel"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"The overnight after the ferry leaves (converted-casona boutique)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"premier","source":"https://cuppatocopatravels.com/south-america/uruguay/colonia-del-sacramento-guide-uruguay/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"boutique bedbank 10–18% / consortia","wells":["stay","move","shop"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":18,"commission_lane":["consortia"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Buenos Aires day-ferry framing (romantic day-escape / overnight)","si_tag":"romance","tier":"comfort","source":"https://www.getyourguide.","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","si":"romance","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"ferry package / affiliate 4–10%","wells":["stay","move"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["romance"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"destination","culture":"destination","romance":"primary"},"commission_pct_low":4,"commission_pct_high":10,"commission_lane":["package","affiliate"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"},{"name":"Carmelo Tannat wine day — Narbona + Bodega Cordano","si_tag":"culinary","tier":"premier","source":"https://matadornetwork.com/read/uruguay-wine-country/","timing":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"the ~80 km up-river wine sub-region built on Tannat, Uruguay''s national grape. Narbona","si":"culinary","blurb":"the ~80 km up-river wine sub-region built on Tannat, Uruguay''s national grape. Narbona","when":"summer Dec–Feb  + spring/fall shoulders","commission":"DMC/guided wine day w/ transport 10–20% / affiliate 4–8%","wells":["eat"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — si (unambiguous spend type)","si_all":["culinary"],"shelf_fit":{"culinary":"primary","culture":"destination","romance":"destination"},"commission_pct_low":10,"commission_pct_high":20,"commission_lane":["DMC","affiliate","guide"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"band+lane"}],"faq":[{"q":"What is there to do in Colonia del Sacramento''s Barrio Histórico?","a":"You can cover Colonia''s UNESCO Barrio Histórico on foot in about 4–5 hours including lunch: walk the ~12-block grid, the 1700s-era Calle de los Suspiros, the Plaza Mayor house-museums, and the Portón de Campo drawbridge gate, then climb the 111-step lighthouse for river-and-town views. It is compact because the Portuguese laid it out in 1680.","source":"guruguay.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"Is Colonia worth an overnight, or just a day trip?","a":"Worth the overnight — that is the town''s quiet secret. Most travelers arrive on the day-ferry from Buenos Aires, so staying a night gives you the emptied cobbles at dusk and dawn and a sunset on the Rambla as the Río de la Plata turns copper. Book ahead: the top boutique, Charco, has only 8 rooms.","source":"cuppatocopatravels.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you do a wine day from Colonia del Sacramento?","a":"Yes — the wine day runs ~80 km up-river to Carmelo, Uruguay''s Tannat sub-region, with estate lunches at Narbona (a 1909-founded estate) and Bodega Cordano. Book it guided or with a driver: the fire to plan around is drink-and-drive on rural roads.","source":"matadornetwork.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culinary"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Colonia?","a":"Footing, not crime. The single most common visitor injury is a twist or fall on the Barrio Histórico''s uneven 300-year-old cobbles, which turn slick in the wet. Wear closed, gripped footwear and take extra care in rain and after dark — unguided walking is otherwise fine. Tap water is potable, and 911 is the nationwide emergency line.","source":"guruguay.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Do I need my passport for the Buenos Aires day-ferry?","a":"Yes — the crossing is an Argentina→Uruguay international border, and it is the single most common trip-planning error. Passengers clear immigration and customs at the terminal before boarding and check-in closes early, so arrive 1.5–2 hours before departure with your passport for both legs.","source":"directferries.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Colonia del Sacramento, Uruguay — UNESCO Barrio Histórico, the Lighthouse & a Carmelo Wine Day | TravelWell","search_language":"es-UY","local_keywords":["Colonia del Sacramento qué hacer","Barrio Histórico Colonia","Carmelo bodegas","ferry Buenos Aires Colonia","Calle de los Suspiros","Faro de Colonia del Sacramento","Tannat Uruguay","Rambla Colonia atardecer"],"hreflang":["en","es-UY"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/uruguay","read":"2026-08-20T14:55:24Z","source_updated":"2025-12-10T13:00:39+00:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":null,"ultra":[{"name":"Narbona Wine Lodge","brand":"Relais & Châteaux","area":"Carmelo (~80 km / ~1 hr from Colonia)","product":"5-room ultra-boutique estate, king rooms + private terraces, pool, winery, restaurant, Puerto Camacho boat access","earning":"Virtuoso/Fora consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Carmelo Resort & Spa","brand":"Hyatt Unbound Collection","area":"Carmelo (~1 hr from Colonia)","product":"44 keys incl. 24 bi-level suites + 20 detached villas, spa, tennis, indoor pool","earning":"Hyatt Privé / consortia commission + amenities; MoR via consortium/DMC","tier":"ultra"},{"name":"Charco Hotel","area":"Barrio Histórico, Colonia (riverfront, ~10-min walk from ferry port)","product":"8-room design boutique in converted original 1680 Portuguese houses, on-site restaurant + patio","earning":"consortia (Fora/Virtuoso where listed) + bedbank premium; MoR via consortium/bedbank","tier":"premier"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Colonia del Sacramento, Uruguay, Uruguay"},"geo":{"lat":-34.4718,"lng":-57.8446},"orbit":[{"id":"punta-del-este-uruguay","jewels":12,"si":["tropical","romance","culinary"]},{"id":"montevideo-uruguay","jewels":10,"si":["culinary","culture","romance","sports"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 29),
