e state of Zacatecas","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"In Guanajuato: the areas south-west of road 45D","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"FCDO advises against all but essential travel to the areas south-west of road 45D. (San Miguel de Allende and Guanajuato City sit outside this area.)"},{"name":"The state of Michoacán","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Morelia via federal toll roads 15D, 126 and 43","toll road 48D between Morelia and its airport","the town of Pátzcuaro via toll roads 14D and 15 from Morelia, and boat trips on Lake Pátzcuaro","Federal Highway 15D"]},{"name":"In Jalisco: the areas south and south-west of Lake Chapala to the Colima border","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Thirty-nine named municipalities, including Autlán de Navarro, Sayula, Tapalpa, Cocula and Villa Corona — the advisory lists each by name."},{"name":"In Jalisco: eleven northern municipalities","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"Bolaños, Chimaltitán, Colotlán, Hostotipaquillo, Huejúcar, Huequilla el Alto, Mezquitic, San Martín de Bolaños, Santa María de los Ángeles, Totatiche and Villa Guerrero."},{"name":"The state of Colima","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the city of Manzanillo by sea, or by air via Manzanillo-Costalegre International Airport","direct travel via road 200 from that airport to Manzanillo"]},{"name":"The state of Guerrero, including the city of Acapulco","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","except":["the town of Zihuatanejo/Ixtapa accessed by air"]},{"name":"Within 40km of the Guatemalan border, from the Pacific Coast up to and including the Gracias a Dios crossing","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential"},{"name":"Federal Highway 199 between Rancho Nuevo, outside San Cristóbal de las Casas, and the Chancalá junction outside Palenque","lvl":3,"posture":"all-but-essential","note":"The restriction is the highway segment, not the towns at either end."}]},"timing":{"peak":"Nov-Apr (dry season, calm, humpbacks Dec-Mar, Careyes polo/events season, ultra-villa demand highest)","shoulder":"May & late Oct (warm, quieter, pre/post rains)","green":"Jul-Oct (hot/humid, emerald hills, hurricane window May-Nov, softer rates)","event_peak":"Careyes polo late-Nov->end-Apr (Agua Alta Cup at Easter); Ondalinda x Careyes Nov 12-15 2026","out_of_season_fill_the_beds":"green season (Jul-Oct) eco/wildlife (turtle nesting, biosphere), sportfishing, storm-quiet villa buyouts at softer rates - the ''secret season''","sources":["https://mexiconewsdaily.com/travel/an-insiders-guide-to-the-perfect-weekend-in-costalegre/","https://www.ondalinda.com/festivals/careyes/","https://www.costalegre.ca/"],"fire_date":"content-only - no campaign; if founder rules carve-out for private-airstrip enclaves, open winter/holiday villa campaigns in spring for following Nov-Apr peak (6-12-mo lead)","event_peaks":"Christmas-New Year (ultra premium), Semana Santa/Easter (Agua Alta Cup polo), Ondalinda (mid-Nov), winter polo season","booking_lead":"ultra villas for Christmas-New Year/winter holidays book 6-12 months ahead, contracted direct on application; green-season windows far shorter"},"jewels":[{"name":"Careyes clifftop Castles & Iconic Villas","si_tag":"Luxury / Ultra-Luxury","status":"future","tier":"ultra","bookable":"Careyes reservations / villa specialist","source":"https://careyes.com/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"staffed clifftop villas with moat-like infinity pools; Heidi Klum married here, celebrities vacation here","si":"ultra","blurb":"staffed clifftop villas with moat-like infinity pools; Heidi Klum married here, celebrities vacation here","when":"year-round","commission":"on application / villa specialist","wells":["stay"],"wells_basis":"derived from name/blurb/hook","si_all":["ultra"],"shelf_fit":{"ocean":"destination","romance":"destination","tropical":"destination","ultra":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,