embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane"},{"name":"Baños de Cuenca thermal circuit — Piedra de Agua","si_tag":"RHN / Wellness","tier":"essential","source":"https://travelwritingpro.com/piedra-de-agua-hot-springs-spa-banos-de-cuenca-ecuador/","timing":"year-round","timing_type":"ALWAYS-ON","hook":"Volcanic hot springs 20 min from downtown, water surfacing at ~75°C and cooled to a bathing 36–40°C","si":"romance","blurb":"Volcanic hot springs 20 min from downtown, water surfacing at ~75°C and cooled to a bathing 36–40°C","when":"year-round","commission":"DMC add-on / spa entry pass-through + transfer","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["RHN / Wellness","romance","wellness"],"shelf_fit":{"RHN / Wellness":"evidenced","culture":"destination","romance":"primary","wellness":"evidenced"},"commission_lane":["DMC"],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"lane","si_raw":"RHN / Wellness","si_map_basis":"normalised from free text ''RHN / Wellness'' by gen_normalise_jewel_si"}],"faq":[{"q":"What makes Cuenca a UNESCO World Heritage city?","a":"Its historic center is a living colonial grid crowned by the New Cathedral — the Catedral de la Inmaculada Concepción, whose three blue-and-white domes were tiled with glaze from old Czechoslovakia and whose towers were left truncated by a load-bearing miscalculation. Built from 1885 over nearly a century, it is free to enter, with dome access monetized.","source":"en.wikipedia.org, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture-&-heritage-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Ingapirca worth the day trip from Cuenca?","a":"Yes — it is Ecuador''s largest Inca ruin, ~80 km north (~3,150 m), a rare Inca-Cañari blend crowned by the elliptical Temple of the Sun, the only one of its kind in the empire, built atop a Cañari sacred rock. Go guided full-day (highest margin) or self-serve by Transportes Cañar bus (~$3.50).","source":"happygringo.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture-&-heritage-—-future-si"},{"q":"Is Cuenca a good romantic honeymoon base?","a":"Yes — it is a gentle, walkable heritage-city honeymoon, not a beach one. Restored 19th-century casonas like Mansión Alcázar (three blocks from Parque Calderón, with garden, spa and fine dining) and Hotel Santa Lucía anchor the boutique-colonial base, with the Baños de Cuenca thermal circuit — water surfacing at ~75°C — 20 minutes out.","source":"travelwritingpro.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"Can you hike El Cajas from Cuenca on your own?","a":"Only partly — go guided beyond the marked loops. El Cajas (28,000 ha, 786 lakes) has no cell signal and weather that turns in minutes; only the Laguna Toreadora and Laguna Llaviucu loops are well marked, and exposure deaths have occurred on unmarked trails. The ~2-hour Toreadora loop (~3,960 m) is self-guided-feasible for the acclimatized.","source":"moontravelguides.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for in Cuenca?","a":"Altitude, not crime. Cuenca sits at ~2,560 m, just above the 2,500 m AMS threshold — effects are usually mild and pass in 2–3 days — but El Cajas hiking at ~3,960–4,000 m is genuine high-altitude exertion. Take a slow first day, hydrate 3+ L/day, skip alcohol early, and do Cajas after a day or two in the city rather than on arrival.","source":"mytrip2ecuador.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Is El Cajas dangerous?","a":"It can be if you go off-trail unprepared — exposure deaths have occurred there. The park has no cell signal and weather changes in minutes; only the Toreadora and Llaviucu loops are well marked. Guided is strongly preferred beyond those two loops; carry layers, a rain shell, water and food regardless of forecast, and hike after acclimatizing.","source":"moontravelguides.com, 2026-07-07","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Cuenca & the Southern Andes, Ecuador — Travel Guide, El Cajas, Ingapirca & Panama Hats | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-EC","local_keywords":["qué hacer 