at and carries everything in and out.","source":"islands.com / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"wildlife"},{"q":"How do I visit if the sea lions are closed?","a":"Come for the empty island itself — pink-cliff coves, white-sand beaches, kayak/SUP and the San Rafaelito reef snorkel that substitutes for Los Islotes in summer. Private crewed sailing charters (from ~$600+ per boat) are the calmest way to see it.","source":"thoroughlytravel.com / scubaboard.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"ocean"},{"q":"What''s the real risk on an uninhabited island?","a":"No services, no cell signal and no medical facilities. Any emergency requires a boat back to La Paz, then Hospital Salvatierra or private clinics with air-evac for major trauma — so carry travel medical + evacuation insurance and bring your own water, food and sun protection.","source":"hgejms.gob.mx / thoroughlytravel.com, 2026-07-04","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Espíritu Santo Island: UNESCO Sea-of-Cortez Guide","meta_description":"Snorkel with sea lions at Los Islotes and land on uninhabited, UNESCO-listed Espíritu Santo from La Paz — permits, seasons (colony closed Jun–Aug) and how to book.","slug":"espiritu-santo-island-mexico","primary_keyword":"Espíritu Santo island","long_tail":["Espiritu Santo tour from La Paz","Los Islotes sea lion snorkel season","Espiritu Santo CONANP permit","Camp Cecil glamping Espiritu Santo","uninhabited island Sea of Cortez"],"search_language":["en","es-MX"],"local_keywords":["Isla Espíritu Santo tour desde La Paz","nadar con lobos marinos Los Islotes","permiso CONANP Isla Espíritu Santo","Parque Nacional Archipiélago Espíritu Santo","campamento Camp Cecil Espíritu Santo","snorkel Mar de Cortés isla deshabitada"],"hreflang":["en","es-MX"],"jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","content_freshness":"2026-07-04","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Orga