embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"},{"name":"León day trip","si_tag":"culture","tier":"essential","source":"https://bbqboy.net/visiting-granada-volcan-masaya-and-laguna-de-apoyo-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07","timing":"Nov–Apr","when_source":"derived from destination timing","timing_type":"SEASONAL-WINDOW","hook":"Granada''s colonial rival/sibling city, an easy day out for churches and revolutionary-mural history","si":"culture","blurb":"Granada''s colonial rival/sibling city, an easy day out for churches and revolutionary-mural history","when":"Nov–Apr","commission":"dormant","accessed":"2026-07-07","wells":["activities"],"wells_basis":"pass 2 — text","si_all":["culture"],"shelf_fit":{"culture":"primary"},"commission_lane":[],"commission_embedded":false,"commission_basis":"unparsed"}],"faq":[{"q":"Why is Granada worth visiting?","a":"Granada is the oldest city in Nicaragua and the oldest colonial city on the American mainland, settled in 1524 by conquistador Francisco Hernández de Córdoba. It claims to be the first European-established city on the mainland of the Americas, and its well-preserved colonial grid of pastel façades is the whole point of coming.","source":"costarica.org, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"culture"},{"q":"What are the best outdoor things to do around Granada?","a":"The signature outings are volcanoes and water. Las Isletas — 365 islets flung into Lake Nicaragua by a Mombacho eruption — are toured by boat or kayak; Mombacho''s cloud-forest is reached by 4x4 to a Crater Trail hike plus a canopy zip course; and Masaya''s night tour puts you at a crater-rim platform above an active lava lake.","source":"viator.com; tripadvisor.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Where''s the best place to swim near Granada?","a":"Laguna de Apoyo, a crater lake about 25 minutes from Granada, is said to be the cleanest place to swim in all of Nicaragua because no motorboats are allowed on it. Day passes to lakeside spots run around $10 and include kayaks and loungers.","source":"hiddennicaragua.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"expedition"},{"q":"Is Granada a good honeymoon destination?","a":"Yes, on paper it is a natural romance set — private-island lodges, rooftop sunsets over Cocibolca, pastel streets. The ultra anchor is Jicaro Island Lodge, a National Geographic Unique Lodge with 9 two-story \"treehouse\" casitas on a private Las Isletas islet, with lakeside yoga and three multi-course meals included.","source":"jicaroisland.com, Accessed 2026-07-07","si_tag":"romance"},{"q":"What''s the real risk to plan for?","a":"Wrongful detention is the headline gatekeeper. A secondary risk is healthcare: comprehensive care exists only in Managua.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua","si_tag":"safety"},{"q":"Are the volcano hikes and lake trips dangerous?","a":"Mombacho and Masaya are done with a park-authorized or licensed guide (volcanic-gas exposure and timed entry make it mandatory at Masaya), and Las Isletas boating requires lifejackets because Cocibolca can chop up fast.","source":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua","si_tag":"safety"}],"seo":{"meta_title":"Granada, Nicaragua Travel Guide — Colonial Jewel, Las Isletas & Volcanoes | TravelWell.World","jsonld_type":"TouristDestination","search_language":"es-NI","local_keywords":["qué hacer en Granada Nicaragua","Las Isletas","Volcán Masaya","Volcán Mombacho bosque nuboso","Laguna de Apoyo nadar","Catedral de Granada","Calle La Calzada"],"hreflang":["en","es-NI"],"primary_keyword":"Granada","attribution":{"author":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"publisher":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World LLC"},"reviewed_by":{"type":"Organization","name":"TravelWell.World"},"digital_source_type":"CompositeWithTrainedAlgorithmicMediaDigitalSource","digital_source_vocab":"https://schema.org/IPTCDigitalSourceEnumeration","last_verified":"2026-08-20","last_verified_basis":"safety.fcdo.read","verified_against":[{"name":"UK Foreign, Commonwealth & Development Office","url":"https://www.gov.uk/foreign-travel-advice/nicaragua","read":"2026-08-20T14:55:16Z","source_updated":"2025-12-10T13:20:42+00:00"}]},"content_freshness":"2026-07-07"},"booking":{"advisory_updated":"2026-08-20","advisory_authority":"FCDO"},"si_checklist_25":null,"sis_present":[{"si":"culture","status":"live"}],"ultra":[{"name":"Jicaro Island Lodge","note":"NatGeo Unique Lodge, 9 treehouse casitas on private Las Isletas islet, spa/yoga, near-carbon-neutral","price_tier":"$$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://jicaroisland.com/ + Accessed 2026-07-07"},{"name":"Tribal Hotel","note":"boutique retreat in colonial core, garden + pool","price_tier":"$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://www.lightfoottravel.com/us/property/tribal-hotel + Accessed 2026-07-07"},{"name":"La Gran Francia / Hotel Plaza Colón","note":"restored colonial-mansion luxury on/near Parque Central","price_tier":"$$$","commission_path":"dormant","source":"https://voicesoftravel.com/where-to-stay-in-granada-nicaragua/ + Accessed 2026-07-07"}],"source_verified":null,"hero":{"query":"Granada, Nicaragua, Nicaragua"},"geo":{"lat":11.9344,"lng":-85.956},"orbit":[{"id":"ometepe-island-nicaragua","jewels":8,"si":["wellness"]},{"id":"san-juan-del-sur-nicaragua","jewels":7,"si":["tropical","romance"]}],"orbit_country":[]}'::jsonb, 41),
